From 023d97f013a8075766276e7635bf98c8a06c660b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 23:01:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: one navigation, one layout system, web and mobile
 identical

The site had two navigations. The header held three hand-maintained arrays
(mega, primary, mobile) and they had already drifted: a desktop visitor could
not reach /guides, /answers, /glossary, /trade or /contact from the header at
all, while a phone visitor could. The footer held sixteen hand-written <li>
elements in one "Company" column, which is a list, not a structure.

data/navigation.ts is now the only place a navigation link exists. The desktop
mega-menu and the mobile drawer render the same array with the same group
headings in the same order; the footer columns and the mobile footer accordions
do too. The breakpoint changes the presentation, never the site.

Structure follows aws.amazon.com, the reference the site is being held to:

  - a utility bar of secondary links, hours and phone, which on a phone
    becomes the first block of the drawer rather than disappearing
  - three primary sections opening into grouped panels with a promoted
    "most asked for" card
  - a phone header of hamburger / centred wordmark / search, measured at a
    0.0px offset from centre
  - a four-column footer matrix that collapses to <details> disclosures below
    lg, in CSS, so the footer stays a server component and the links exist
    exactly once in the DOM

The mega-menu is now a real disclosure with aria-expanded, Escape, and
click-outside, rather than a CSS group-hover div that announced itself to a
screen reader as a link. SiteHeader is a server component; only the menu and
the drawer are client islands, so the nav data no longer ships to the browser
on all 358 pages.

Also fixed, each with the test or audit check that would have caught it:

  - a third container width existed on exactly two pages, so /problems/[slug]
    sat at a different measure than its own siblings
  - the h1 scale had forked into two leading values; not-found.tsx had neither
  - none of the 16 raw <img> elements declared how it loads, so /services
    fetched eight images before the fold
  - six price bands were retyped by hand into /for-agents and into the city
    FAQ template on 32 pages; they now come from priceBandOf()
  - /guides/[slug] emitted BreadcrumbList markup with no breadcrumbs on screen
  - the contact page's search snippet hard-coded the phone number and address
  - the footer rendered "Green Hardwood Ltd.. All rights reserved."
  - only the homepage stepped its section padding at sm:, so hand-rolled heroes
    were tighter than PageHero ones on the same site

122 tests. 358 pages, 358 unique titles, 2,004 JSON-LD blocks, audit clean.
